1
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:19,950
When opening the gas cylinder valve, position yourself so the regulator outlet flow valve is pointing away from your body.

2
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:23,990
Do not put your hand on top of the valve as you open it.

3
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:29,270
Slowly open the valve by hand unless a vendor-supplied tool is required.

4
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:35,270
Check the inlet pressure gauge to ensure it registers the expected value.

5
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:39,670
Contact your laboratory supervisor if pressure is less than expected.

6
00:00:40,630 --> 00:00:48,110
Low cylinder pressure may indicate a near-empty cylinder or a leaking valve which can be a serious safety issue.

7
00:00:48,790 --> 00:00:54,670
Slowly turn the regulator control valve until the regulator pressure is at the desired level.

8
00:00:54,950 --> 00:01:00,390
Do not assume that the maximum scale reading on the gauge is the safe working pressure.

9
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:06,430
Slowly open the outlet flow valve on the regulator to start the gas flow to your system.

10
00:01:07,430 --> 00:01:12,110
Do not use the outlet flow valve to control pressure, only gas flow.

11
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:15,470
Pressure is set with the regulator control valve.

12
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:20,950
After flow is established, the set delivery pressure may decrease slightly.

13
00:01:21,110 --> 00:01:26,910
Check to see that the delivery pressure is as desired and make any necessary adjustments.
